# Line endings.
#
# The repo has always stored these LF (`git ls-files --eol` shows `i/lf`), but with
# `core.autocrlf=true` and no attributes file the WORKING TREE got whatever the checkout
# felt like — which is how `scripts/ue5_freeze_helper.lua` ended up CRLF while
# `scripts/ue5_invoke_helper.lua` stayed LF on the same machine. That divergence is what
# produced `[FREEZEINJECT-CRLF-2026-08-20]`: the freeze helper's 1,137 CRLF endings made
# its byte count disagree with the LF-normalised copy Cheat Engine stores, and the
# post-write check reported a good write as a failure.
#
# Pinning `eol=lf` keeps the checkout matching the index so the two can't drift apart
# again. The code no longer DEPENDS on it — CeLuaHygiene.NormalizeTableFilePayload folds
# the payload before it is handed to CE either way — but a tree that agrees with itself
# is one less thing that behaves differently on a fresh clone.
*.lua text eol=lf

# Lua rigs and the CE table are read by the same tooling.
*.CT   text eol=lf

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EVERYTHING ELSE — added 2026-08-23 after a staged-build session kept having to
# work around this.
#
# THE PROBLEM IS THAT `core.autocrlf` IS MACHINE-LOCAL. Measured on this PC:
# it is unset at --local and --global and `true` at --system, i.e. the
# Git-for-Windows installer default living in C:\Program Files\Git\etc\gitconfig.
# That file is not in the repo and does not travel, so the two development PCs can
# check the same commit out with different line endings. `.gitattributes` DOES
# travel, which is why the rule belongs here rather than in a git config.
#
# The index is already uniform: 1,021 of 1,035 tracked files are `i/lf`. The WORKING
# TREE was not — 339 `w/lf`, 679 `w/crlf`, 3 `w/mixed`. Pinning eol=lf makes the
# checkout match the index everywhere.
#
# ⚠ WHY IT MATTERED, concretely: a file that is `i/lf w/lf` gets REWRITTEN TO CRLF by
# `git checkout`, and `git status` stays CLEAN afterwards because the index is
# unchanged. So `git checkout -- <file>` could not be trusted to revert a staged
# experiment byte-for-byte — every staged row in this session reverted from a byte
# snapshot instead. With eol=lf a checkout is byte-safe again.
#
# `text=auto`, never a bare `text`: it lets git keep auto-detecting binaries, so
# `dll/src/VersionNeedleScan.h` (a deliberate NUL inside a comment about
# NUL-terminated needles) and the image/gz assets are left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never transform, never diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.gz   binary
